title: mark *another's* changes processed
pid: 8c3286a9-5e8d-404d-b90e-fd62221e99e7
body: |2-
  When I read a pruned change view to see your latest changes,
  I can mark yours processed. The experience is probably nearly identical to
  marking changes commit-ready in my own data.
  But those marks should stick around, in my repo,
  until you edit the node again, at which point it will return to my
  set of unprocessed-by-me changes by others.

  You should be able to see whether I processed something of yours.
  (Pronouns here are arbitrary; everything is symmetrical.)
  A user should be able to include or exclude such information
  from the heralds they see.
